"Featured protections"],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Paragraph1",'When it comes to making decisions on where to go, people trust insights and recommendations from others who have been there. Google Maps makes it easy for people to share their knowledge and experiences as a way to help others decide where to go or what business to visit. Every day, we receive millions of posts and updates about places in the form of reviews, photos, videos, and place information like addresses and hours. This <a href="https://blog.google/products/maps/google-maps-101-how-contributed-content-makes-maps-helpful/" target="_blank">user-generated content</a>\u2014along with <a href="https://blog.google/outreach-initiatives/small-business/business-profile-maps-and-search/" target="_blank">updates from businesses</a>, <a href="https://blog.google/products/maps/google-maps-101-how-we-map-world/" target="_blank">data from authoritative sources</a>, and <a href="https://blog.google/products/maps/google-maps-101-how-imagery-powers-our-map/" target="_blank">Google imagery</a>\u2014helps in our ongoing effort to create the freshest, most comprehensive map possible.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Paragraph2",'On Google Maps, people can post <a href="https://support.google.com/maps/answer/6230175" target="_blank">reviews</a> for places they\'ve personally experienced. <a href="./approach" target="_blank">We automatically assess</a> all reviews against our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7422880" target="_blank">content policies</a> before publishing, which includes robust protections against <a href="./protections" target="_blank">fake reviews</a>. To avoid conflicts of interest, business owners and employees are not permitted to submit reviews for their own business or competitors.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Paragraph22026",'On Google Maps, people can post <a href="https://support.google.com/maps/answer/6230175" target="_blank">reviews</a> for places they\'ve personally experienced. <a href="./approach" target="_blank">We automatically assess</a> all reviews against our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7422880" target="_blank">content policies</a> before publishing, which includes robust protections against <a href="./protections" target="_blank">fake reviews</a>. To avoid conflicts of interest, business owners and employees are not permitted to submit or incentivize reviews for their own business or competitors.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Paragraph3",'While most of the 250 million places on Google Maps are eligible for reviews, we may <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/13036130" target="_blank">limit</a> posting on places that are generally not accessible to the public or tend to attract unhelpful, harmful, or off-topic content.'],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Paragraph32026",'While most of the 300 million places on Google Maps are eligible for reviews, we may <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/13036130" target="_blank">limit</a> posting on places that are generally not accessible to the public or tend to attract unhelpful, harmful, or off-topic content.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Paragraph4",'People can post <a href="https://support.google.com/maps/answer/2622947" target="_blank">photos and videos</a> of places on Google Maps, helping others get a genuine sense of the place before they go. We <a href="./approach" target="_blank">automatically assess</a> all user-submitted photos and videos against our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114" target="_blank">content policies</a> before publishing. This includes removing harmful or offensive media like depictions of graphic violence or explicit content, as well as media that diminishes the platform\'s usefulness, such as blurry or overly filtered images.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Paragraph5",'From noticing a new business in the neighborhood to suggesting holiday opening hours, people who are familiar with a place can <a href="https://support.google.com/maps/answer/7084895" target="_blank">suggest an edit</a> in Maps if they notice that information is missing or incorrect. This helps us decide whether to add a new place to the map or update a place\'s information. We <a href="./approach" target="_blank">automatically assess</a> all user-submitted edits against our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114" target="_blank">policies</a> before publishing them. Businesses can help keep their information accurate by <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/7107242" target="_blank">verifying their business</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/3039617" target="_blank">managing their information</a> directly. We prioritize edits from business owners and managers when provided.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Paragraph52026",'From noticing a new business in the neighborhood to suggesting holiday opening hours, people who are familiar with a place can <a href="https://support.google.com/maps/answer/7084895" target="_blank">suggest an edit</a> in Maps if they notice that information is missing or incorrect. This helps us decide whether to add a new place to the map or update a place\'s information. We <a href="./approach" target="_blank">automatically assess</a> all user-submitted edits against our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114" target="_blank">policies</a> before publishing them. Businesses can help keep their information accurate by <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/7107242" target="_blank">verifying their Business Profile</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/3039617" target="_blank">managing their information</a> directly. We prioritize edits from business owners and managers when provided.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Text1","Content and information you can trust"],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Text2","Transparency into content removals on Google Maps"],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Text3","Learn more about how we fight fake reviews and keep Maps helpful"],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Metric1","Total reviews published"],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Metric2","Total photos and videos published"],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Metric2Description","Total number of photos and videos published by users on Google Maps and Search during the selected year."],
["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Metric3","Total place edits published"],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Table1Description","Total number of Local Reviews published on Google Maps and Search during the selected year. Ranking reflects the categories of places with the highest number of published reviews."],["transparencyReport.maps.overview.Table2Description","Total number of place edits published by users on Google Maps and Search during the selected year. One edit may contain multiple attributes (for example, if a person is adding a missing place, they could suggest its name, location and category in a single edit). Ranking reflects the attributes most frequently published."],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.MastheadTitle","Trustworthy content and information"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.MastheadDescription","With more than 2 billion users turning to Google Maps each month, we work hard so people can trust the posts and edits shared by our community.  Our approach reflects our commitment to providing users with access to timely updates, while preventing harm and delivering reliable information."],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Header1","Set clear standards"],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Header2","Protect you from harm"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Header3","Deliver reliable information"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Header4","Partner to advance trust online"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Header5","Deep dive: the journey of a review"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Subheader1","Post"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Subheader2","Detect"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Subheader3","Publish"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Subheader4",
"Monitor"],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Paragraph1",'On Google Maps, people can share content and information about places they experience in the real world. <b>We\u2019ve designed our policies to maximize the helpfulness, accuracy and authenticity of information on our platform</b>, benefiting consumers and businesses alike. We strictly <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114" target="_blank">prohibit</a> fake or misleading reviews, inaccurate information, and other forms of harmful content. See our tips for <a href="https://support.google.com/maps/answer/10357321" target="_blank">posting reviews</a>, <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7411351" target="_blank">photos and videos</a> on Google Maps.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Paragraph2",'We protect people and businesses by automatically assessing all user-submitted content against our policies. <b>Built-in, advanced protection systems block or remove the majority of policy-violating content before anyone sees it</b>. To do this at scale, we use a combination of automated tools and specially trained human operators and analysts. When we detect a heightened risk of abuse, we may deploy <a href="./protections?lu=additional-safeguards" target="_blank">additional safeguards</a>, such as restricting submissions entirely for a period of time.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Paragraph3",'We help people make informed decisions by delivering reliable information and updates from the community and from businesses themselves. <b>Businesses can <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/7107242" target="_blank">verify</a> their listing, respond to reviews, and keep their information up-to-date</b>. People benefit from a wide range of perspectives, with the ability to filter reviews by date or topic to find the most useful information for their specific need. <b>We provide added context to help people evaluate content</b>, such as showing an <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/15178562" target="_blank">alert</a> when we detect suspicious activity, and offer tools for the community to <a href="./enforcement?section=report" target="_blank">report</a> potentially problematic content or behavior.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Paragraph32026",'We help people make informed decisions by delivering reliable information and updates from the community and from businesses themselves. <b>Businesses can <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/7107242" target="_blank">verify</a> their listing, respond to reviews, and keep their information up-to-date</b>. People benefit from a wide range of perspectives, with the ability to access helpful summaries or explore reviews by rating, date or topic. <b>We provide added context to help people evaluate content</b>, such as showing an <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/15178562" target="_blank">alert</a> when we detect suspicious activity, and offer tools for the community to <a href="./enforcement?section=report" target="_blank">report</a> potentially problematic content or behavior.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Paragraph4",'We take a collaborative approach to content trust and safety, sharing our <a href="https://www.regulations.gov/comment/FTC-2022-0070-0034" target="_blank">insights</a> and <a href="https://transparencyreport.google.com/report-downloads?lu=report-27" target="_blank">data</a> to combat fake reviews and other deceptive practices. We may also take <a href="https://blog.google/outreach-initiatives/public-policy/legal-action-stop-fake-review-scams/" target="_blank">legal action</a> against bad actors who attempt to manipulate online platforms and undermine trust between people and businesses.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Paragraph42026",'We take a collaborative, ecosystem-wide approach to content trust and safety. We share <a href="https://www.regulations.gov/comment/FTC-2022-0070-0034" target="_blank">insights</a> and <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/safety-security/the-new-global-signal-exchange-will-help-fight-scams-and-fraud/" target="_blank">data</a> with industry partners and experts to better protect users against deceptive practices. We may also take legal action against bad actors who attempt to manipulate online platforms, such as our litigation to shut down <a href="https://blog.google/outreach-initiatives/public-policy/legal-action-stop-fake-review-scams/" target="_blank">fake review networks</a> and <a href="https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/69755158/google-llc-v-asayag/" target="_blank">fraudulent business scams</a>.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Paragraph5","Reviews on Google Maps are often published in as little as a few seconds, but behind the scenes, there\u2019s a lot going on in our mission to publish trustworthy content. Here\u2019s a look at how user-submitted content makes its way onto Google Maps."],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Text1",'Whether you\u2019re submitting directly on Google Maps or from Google Search, our moderation systems spring into action the moment you hit "post".'],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Text2",
'Our first line of defense against content that violates our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7422880" target="_blank">policies</a> is our advanced machine learning models. These models excel at identifying patterns to help determine if content is authentic or violates any of our policies. As a result, the majority of fake and policy-violating reviews (over 85%) are <b>blocked or removed before anyone actually sees them</b>.'],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Text22026",
'Our first line of defense against content that violates our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7422880" target="_blank">policies</a> is our advanced machine learning models. These models excel at identifying patterns to help determine if content is authentic or violates any of our policies. As a result, the majority of fake and policy-violating reviews are <b>blocked or removed before anyone actually sees them</b>.'],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Text3",'When assessing content, our models look at the posts or edits from multiple angles, such as:<ul><li><b>The content itself:</b> Does it contain profanity, explicit imagery or other <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114" target="_blank">prohibited content</a>?<li><b>The account that posted the content:</b> Does the Google account have any history of suspicious or policy-violating behavior?<li><b>The place itself:</b> Has there been unusual activity \u2014 such as an abundance of reviews or edits over a short period of time? Has it recently gotten attention in the news or on social media that would motivate people to try to manipulate the business profile?</ul>'],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Text4","In addition to our automated systems, we have a global team of human operators and analysts available to support with content evaluations. Their expertise is helpful when automated systems have difficulty, like with reviews using local slang. <b>We combine these human insights with machine learning to continuously improve how we enforce our policies</b>. This helps us quickly remove policy violations and reduces the risk of removing legitimate reviews."],
["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Text5",'If no policy violations are found, content is published. Your reviews, ratings, photos and videos are publicly visible when you search for a place, and can also be found on your Google Maps contribution <a href="https://support.google.com/maps/answer/9320433" target="_blank">profile</a>.'],["transparencyReport.maps.approach.Text6",'Even after content is published, we continue to monitor for suspicious activity. For example, if an account posts the same review multiple times, or we discover that a review is part of a paid review network, we will take action by removing previously published content and potentially suspending the account for policy-violating behavior. We also encourage the community to <a href="./enforcement?section=report" target="_blank">report</a> inappropriate content and behavior, adding to our multi-layered approach.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.MastheadTitle","Google Maps User-Generated Content Policy Enforcement"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.MastheadDescription",'We rigorously enforce our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7422880?ref_topic=7422769" target="_blank">content policies</a> in order to reduce the risk of harm and keep the information on Maps relevant and helpful.'],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Header1","Reporting and appeals"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Subheader1",
"Content removed"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Subheader2","Accounts restricted"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Subheader3","Business Profiles removed"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Subheader4","Report content"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Subheader5","Report an account"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Subheader6","Submit an appeal"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Paragraph1","This exhibit shows the number of reviews, photos, videos, and edits blocked or removed due to policy violations annually.  When a review is removed, all accompanying content (for example, star rating, photos or videos) is also removed."],
["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Paragraph2",'Learn more about how we <a href="./protections?lu=fighting-fake-reviews" target="_blank">fight fake reviews</a> and <a href="./protections?lu=keeping-content-helpful" target="_blank">keep Maps helpful</a>.'],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Paragraph3",'Accounts that repeatedly or severely violate our policies <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/13780814" target="_blank">may lose access to features</a>, such as the ability to post. If an account is restricted from posting reviews, all past reviews will also be removed.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Paragraph4",'We protect users and businesses from abuse by removing fake and fraudulent <a href="https://business.google.com/" target="_blank">Business Profiles</a>. This exhibit shows the number of Business Profiles removed for violating our <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/3038177" target="_blank">guidelines for representing a business</a> on Google Maps, such as cases of <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114?sjid=11550358951995581628-NA#zippy=%2Cmisrepresentation%2Cmisinformation%2Cimpersonation" target="_blank">impersonation or scams</a>. While most violations are automatically detected and removed by our internal systems, reports from the Google Maps community also help us identify violations.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Paragraph5",'We encourage Google Maps users to report any content or behavior that violates our policies. <b>We won\'t remove content simply because a user or business dislikes it</b> \u2014 we rely on our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7422880" target="_blank">content policies</a> and applicable local laws to guide removal decisions. Reports of policy violations from the community provide valuable signals to our teams to investigate.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Text1","See something that doesn't look right? Here are different ways that you can help."],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Text2","If you notice an account is engaging in fraudulent or inappropriate behavior, let us know."],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Text22026","If you notice an account or entity is engaging in fraudulent or inappropriate behavior, let us know."],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Text3","If you believe action was taken on your content or account in error, you may be able to appeal."],
["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Metric1","Total reviews removed"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Metric2","Total photos and videos removed"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Metric3","Total place edits removed"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Metric3Description","Total number of user submissions for the selected year that were blocked or removed due to policy violations, applicable law, or a user's request."],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Metric4","Total accounts restricted"],
["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Metric4Description","Total number of accounts with posting restrictions applied during the selected year."],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Metric5","Total business profiles removed"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Metric5Description","Total number of fake or fraudulent Business Profiles blocked or removed during the selected year."],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Chart1","Reviews removed, by reason"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Chart1Description",
'Reviews removed as a percentage of total reviews contributed. <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Cfake-engagement%2Cimpersonation%2Cmisinformation%2Cmisrepresentation" target="_blank">Fake or misleading reviews</a> violate policies related to fake engagement. <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Cviolence-and-gore%2Coffensive-content%2Cpersonal-information%2Cobscenity-profanity%2Cadult-themed-content%2Coff-topic%2Cunclear-and-repetitive-content%2Cdefacement-mischief%2Cunclear-content%2Crepetitive-content" target="_blank">Vandalism</a> includes policy violations such as profanity, repetitive and off-topic content. <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/13780814" target="_blank">Account restriction</a> refers to past reviews removed due to an account-level restriction. <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Csexually-explicit-content%2Cviolence-and-gore%2Chate-speech%2Charassment%2Cdangerous-content%2Cterrorist-content%2Cillegal-content%2Cchild-safety%2Cviolence-gore" target="_blank">Harm</a> includes violations such as harassment, hate speech and illegal content.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Chart1Description2026",'Reviews removed as a percentage of total reviews contributed. <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Cfake-engagement%2Cimpersonation%2Cmisinformation%2Cmisrepresentation" target="_blank">Fake or misleading reviews</a> violate policies related to fake engagement and rating manipulation. <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Cviolence-and-gore%2Coffensive-content%2Cpersonal-information%2Cobscenity-profanity%2Cadult-themed-content%2Coff-topic%2Cunclear-and-repetitive-content%2Cdefacement-mischief%2Cunclear-content%2Crepetitive-content" target="_blank">Vandalism</a> includes policy violations such as profanity, repetitive and off-topic content. <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/13780814" target="_blank">Account restriction</a> refers to past reviews removed due to an account-level restriction. <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Csexually-explicit-content%2Cviolence-and-gore%2Chate-speech%2Charassment%2Cdangerous-content%2Cterrorist-content%2Cillegal-content%2Cchild-safety%2Cviolence-gore" target="_blank">Harm</a> includes violations such as harassment, hate speech and illegal content.'],
