"Report a third-party agency"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Link72","Report a review extortion scam"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Link8","Appeal an enforcement action"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Link9","Appeal a business restriction"],["transparencyReport.maps.enforcement.Obs1","*Appeal options may vary based on violation or location."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.MastheadTitle","Featured protections"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.MastheadDescription",
"Here we highlight some of our built-in protections that help keep user-generated content on Google Maps helpful and reliable."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Subheader1","How we detect fake reviews"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Subheader2","Responding to businesses that engage in fake reviews"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Subheader22026","Responding to businesses that engage in fake and incentivized reviews"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Subheader3","Examples of inappropriate content"],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Subheader4","How we detect inappropriate content"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Subheader5","Temporary restrictions"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Subheader6","Long-term protections"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Subheader7","Looking ahead"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph1","Fake and misleading reviews are an industry-wide challenge that can erode trust and undermine the usefulness of online platforms. We take swift action against fake reviews and invest heavily in protections to remove them from Google Maps."],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph2",'<a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Cfake-engagement" target="_blank">Fake engagement</a> can take many forms. Some reviews are simply fabricated, written by people who never visited the business. Others are attempts to manipulate ratings, such as a business soliciting positive reviews in exchange for money or discounts, or offering incentives to get consumers to remove or revise negative feedback. Reviews can also be manipulated by individuals creating multiple accounts to sabotage or boost a place\u2019s rating. <b>Broadly speaking, we do not permit any content that does not reflect a genuine experience at the place in question</b>.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph3","Detecting fake engagement is a complex policy enforcement challenge, as it\u2019s rarely obvious simply by looking at the content of the review. To address this, we utilize a variety of cutting-edge tools and techniques."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph4","Most fake reviews are immediately detected and removed by our systems. Our machine learning models are trained on extensive datasets of both known fake and genuine reviews, which enables them to <b>identify patterns and anomalies indicative of fraudulent activity</b>. Our models analyze multiple factors, including account-level context to spot potential connections to other suspicious accounts and paid review operations, as well as patterns at the place itself, such as a sudden influx of 5-star reviews or situations where a conflict of interest or incentive may result in a biased review."],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph42026","Most fake reviews are immediately detected and removed by our systems. Our machine learning models are trained on extensive datasets of both fake and genuine reviews, to <b>identify patterns indicative of fraudulent activity</b>. We also train them to reason like a skilled analyst\u2014breaking the evaluation into steps to understand <em>why</em> a review is likely to be abusive before making a final decision. This allows us to distinguish fake reviews from genuine ones with more nuance and precision."],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph422026","For example, our models analyze account-level context to spot potential connections to other suspicious accounts and paid review operations. They also examine activity at the place itself, looking for anomalies like a sudden influx of 1 or 5-star reviews, or situations where a conflict of interest or incentive may result in biased reviews."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph5","If a review is flagged by our community, we may also rely on our highly trained team of content reviewers to make a decision based on our policies."],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph52026","If a review is flagged by our community, we may also rely on our highly trained team of content reviewers and analysts  to make a decision based on our policies. This layer of review is especially valuable for investigating the most complex cases or serious threats."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph6","While we\u2019ve made significant progress in this area, we know that scammers continue to evolve \u2014 and we will too. Our teams continue working around the clock and investing in the latest technology to keep contributed content on Google Maps authentic and reliable."],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph62026","While we\u2019ve made significant progress in this area, we know that scammers continue to evolve \u2014 and we will too. We regularly retrain our models and invest in new technologies to protect against new threats. Our teams work around the clock to keep contributed content on Google Maps authentic and reliable."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph7",'We take fake and incentivized reviews on businesses very seriously. If a Business Profile is repeatedly found to violate our fake engagement policy, we may place <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/14114287" target="_blank">restrictions</a> on it, in addition to removing the fake reviews. Restrictions can include anything from not being eligible to receive new reviews to unpublishing all existing reviews for a set period of time.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph72026",'We take fake and incentivized reviews on businesses very seriously. If a Business Profile is found to violate our fake engagement policy, we may place <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/14114287" target="_blank">restrictions</a> on it, in addition to removing the fake reviews. Restrictions range from not being eligible to receive new reviews to unpublishing all existing reviews for a set period of time.'],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph8",
'<b>We\'re also continually rolling out new measures to increase consumer trust and crack down on those who try to cheat the system.</b> For example, when a Business Profile has a restriction applied, a <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/15178562" target="_blank">consumer alert</a> will appear on the page to let people know that suspicious reviews have been identified and removed.'],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph82026",'When a Business Profile has a restriction applied, an <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/15178562" target="_blank">alert</a> will appear on the page to let people know that suspicious reviews have been identified and removed. This transparency helps deter deceptive practices and provides context so consumers can make informed decisions.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph9","Owners of claimed Business Profiles are notified of restrictions and have the opportunity to appeal the decision if they believe our evaluation is incorrect. Our team of analysts oversees the restrictions process carefully so that they are applied appropriately."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph92026",'Owners of <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/7107242" target="_blank">verified</a> Business Profiles are notified of restrictions and have the opportunity to appeal the decision if they believe our evaluation is incorrect. Our team of analysts oversees the restrictions process carefully so that they are applied appropriately.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph10","These measures help create a level playing field for businesses on Google Maps."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph11",'<b>Inappropriate content</b> categories include things like harassment, which we remove to protect users and businesses, as well as content that is "off-topic"\u2014that is, not directly related to a first-hand experience at a specific place. For example, during times of political conflict, we sometimes see restaurants around the world vandalized with one-star reviews simply because of their cuisine type. We\u2019ve also seen situations where a business gets flooded with off-topic reviews related to a recent news story about the owner, even if the reviewers haven\'t actually had a personal experience with the place. Content like this diminishes the usefulness of our platform and is removed in accordance with our policies.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph12",'Our advanced learning models are trained to identify inappropriate content that falls within our <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114" target="_blank">prohibited categories</a>. However, language is nuanced, and what might be acceptable in one <a href="https://blog.google/products/maps/how-google-maps-reviews-work/#:~:text=Training%20a%20machine,from%20going%20live." target="_blank">context</a> could violate our policies in another. Our human analysts bring their expertise to these complex cases, conducting assessments across languages and cultures, and continually refining our systems for better accuracy.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph13",'Additionally, the broader Maps community plays an important role in reporting inappropriate content. Businesses can <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/4596773" target="_blank">report</a> policy-violating reviews posted on their Business Profiles and check the status of reports in the <a href="https://support.google.com/business/workflow/9945796" target="_blank">reviews management tool</a>. Google Maps users can also report policy-violating reviews following the steps listed <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7445749#zippy=%2Creport-inappropriate-content%2Creport-inappropriate-reviews%2Cto-report-review" target="_blank">here</a>.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph14","While our automated systems are effective at catching a wide range of violations, there are certain situations where we go a step further to safeguard the people and businesses on our platform."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph15","There are times when certain places or geographic areas become vulnerable to an influx of irrelevant, offensive, or malicious content. This could be in response to a real-world event that attracts off-topic comments, a coordinated effort to manipulate a place\u2019s ratings, or even a larger geographic area that may be at higher risk due to conflict or instability."],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph16",'In addition to taking down policy-violating content, we may proactively apply additional protections, such as a <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/15178562" target="_blank">banner</a> on the place page letting people know that unusual activity has been detected and suspicious reviews were removed.'],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph17",'We may also <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/13036130#zippy=%2Cshort-term-restrictions" target="_blank">temporarily restrict</a> posting to prevent further abuse.  When this happens, we monitor the place and when we see the abuse attempts and the risk of policy-violating content subside, we lift the restrictions.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph18",'We have instituted <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/13036130#zippy=%2Clong-term-restrictions" target="_blank">long-term protections</a> for places where we have found user contributions to be consistently unhelpful, harmful, or off-topic. This includes categories of places where people typically don\u2019t have a choice about which location to go to or places only accessible to people stationed or assigned there, such as police stations and prisons. In designing these protections, we evaluate how helpful community input might be for these types of places, and based on the outcome we may apply restrictions ranging from limiting contributions to blocking a specific type of content to blocking user-generated content altogether.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph19","The landscape for user-generated content is constantly shifting, with new technologies like generative AI, evolving abuse trends, and global events creating fresh challenges each year. That's why we\u2019re continually refining our policies, strengthening our enforcement systems, expanding our collaboration with others in the industry, and increasing transparency."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph20","We are confident that our ongoing investments in policy, detection, and enforcement will position us to address the challenges ahead. We remain deeply committed to fostering trust and ensuring that Google Maps continues to be a reliable and helpful resource for everyone."],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Paragraph21",'In addition to our robust protections against <a href="./protections?lu=fighting-fake-reviews" target="_blank">fake engagement</a>, we enforce our policies on <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114" target="_blank">inappropriate content and behavior</a> so that the information people find on Google Maps is <b>helpful and relevant</b>.'],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Metric1","Fake and misleading reviews removed"],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Metric1Description",'Total number of Local Reviews removed for violating our policies related to <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Cfake-engagement%2Cimpersonation%2Cmisinformation%2Cmisrepresentation" target="_blank">fake engagement</a>.'],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Metric2","Reviews removed for vandalism or off-topic content"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Metric2Description",'Total number of Local Reviews removed for violating policies related to <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Cviolence-and-gore%2Coffensive-content%2Cpersonal-information%2Cobscenity-profanity%2Cadult-themed-content%2Coff-topic%2Cunclear-and-repetitive-content%2Cdefacement-mischief%2Cunclear-content%2Crepetitive-content" target="_blank">vandalism</a>, including profanity, repetitive and off-topic content.'],
["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Metric3","Temporary protections enabled"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Metric3Description","Total number of places with temporary posting restrictions applied during the selected year."],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Metric4","Reviews removed for harmful content"],["transparencyReport.maps.protections.Metric4Description",'Total number of Local Reviews removed for violating policies related to <a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114#zippy=%2Csexually-explicit-content%2Cviolence-and-gore%2Chate-speech%2Charassment%2Cdangerous-content%2Cterrorist-content%2Cillegal-content%2Cchild-safety%2Cviolence-gore" target="_blank">harm</a>, including harassment, hate speech and illegal content.'],
