"Learn more at How YouTube Works"],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.FooterParagraphText1","<i><b>Data Collection Note:</b><br>All data in this report is collected between {startDate} through {endDate}, unless otherwise annotated as below:</i>"],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.FooterParagraphText2","<i>\u2020 Data collected as a 'snapshot' in October 2023. Some data, like rate of counter notifications and Content ID disputes, look at \"trailing\" events. We start with the set of claims or removals made during H1 2023, but disputes and counter notifications continue to accrue after that period because they can be made at any time. For instance, a claim made on May 30, 2023 may have a dispute made on October 1, 2023. For these data points, we have chosen to take a snapshot 3 months after the end of H1 2023.</i>"],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.FooterParagraphText2V6","<i>\u2020 Data collected as a 'snapshot' in {date1}. Some data, like rate of counter notifications and Content ID disputes, look at \"trailing\" events. We start with the set of claims or removals made during {period}, but disputes and counter notifications continue to accrue after that period because they can be made at any time. For instance, a claim made on {date2} may have a dispute made on {date3}. For these data points, we have chosen to take a snapshot 3 months after the end of {period}.</i>"],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.FooterParagraphText3","<i><b>Terminology Note:</b><br>* While in general, claimants must provide evidence that they have initiated court action to prevent a video from being reinstated by counter notification, other forms of valid legal action, such as a Copyright Claims Board complaint, may be accepted</i>"],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.edge.SectionTitle4Component0ParagraphTextV7","Over time, we've also worked to safely expand automated detection technology to more users. All copyright holders can use our webform to ask us to try to automatically prevent copies of the removed content from being reuploaded. In 2024 our automated system prevented over 7 million videos from being uploaded because they copied content from videos removed due to copyright removal requests."],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.edge.SectionTitle4Component0ParagraphTextV8","Over time, we've also worked to safely expand automated detection technology to more users. All copyright holders can use our webform to ask us to try to automatically prevent copies of the removed content from being reuploaded. In 2025 our automated system prevented over 6 million videos from being uploaded because they copied content from videos removed due to copyright removal requests."],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle0Component1ChartTitleV7",
"Ad revenue paid to rightsholders as of December 2024 from content claimed and monetized through Content ID"],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle1Component1ParagraphTextV7","<b>Webform</b><br>In {year1}, <b>over 60% of claimants</b> who claimed or requested removal of content through YouTube's Copyright Management Suite did so through the webform."],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle1Component1HeaderTextV7","Webform"],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle1Component2HeaderTextV7",
"Copyright Match Tool"],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle1Component3HeaderTextV7","Content ID"],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle1Component2ParagraphTextV7","<b>Copyright Match Tool</b><br>As of {date2}, over <b>{copyrightmatchtoolaccesscount} channels have access</b>  to the tool. It automatically detects copies of their content uploaded to other channels."],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle1Component3ParagraphTextV7","<b>Content ID</b><br>Our solution for those with the most complex rights management needs (such as movie studios, record labels, and collecting societies) - <b>over {accessparterncount} partners had access</b> as of {date1}. Although they represent the smallest number of users for any of our tools, claims from Content ID partners represent over <b>99% of all copyright actions</b> on YouTube, totalling <b>over {contentidclaimcount} claims</b> in {year1}. In {year1}, rightsholders chose to monetize <b>over 90%</b> of all Content ID claims."],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.PdfDownloadCenterDescV7",'For previous versions of this report covering January 2021 through December 2022, refer to the <a href="https://transparencyreport.google.com/report-downloads?lu=report-22" target="_blank">PDF Download Center</a>. For 2023 onward, reference the date dropdown on this site.'],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.MastheadDescriptionV7","We build tools that empower users to access, create, and share information like never before \u2014 giving them more choice, opportunity, and exposure to a diversity of viewpoints. <b>Today, billions of logged-in users come to YouTube every month.</b> YouTube has also given rightsholders opportunities to earn money from both their own and user-generated content through our subscription-based and advertising-supported models."],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.intro.SectionTitle0Component0ParagraphTextV7","At YouTube, supporting the free flow of ideas and creativity is core to our mission to give everyone a voice and show them the world. With this in mind, we build tools that empower users to access, create, and share information like never before \u2014 giving them more choice, opportunity, and exposure to a diversity of viewpoints. Today, billions of logged-in users come to YouTube every month."],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.intro.SectionTitle0Component2ParagraphTextV7",
"YouTube has over 125 million Premium and Music subscribers, including trialers, across 100 countries as of March 2025. Through Content ID, YouTube has created an entirely new revenue stream from ad-supported, user-generated content, paying more than $12 billion to rightsholders from ads alone as of December 2024, from content claimed and monetized through the tool."],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.intro.SectionTitle0Group3Component1ChartTitleV7","Ad revenue paid to rightsholders as of December 2024 from content claimed and monetized through Content ID"],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.access.SectionTitle0Component1ParagraphTextV7","<b>Copyright Match Tool:</b> As of {date2}, over {copyrightmatchtoolaccesscount} channels have access to the Copyright Match Tool, which we built for those with more frequent copyright needs. It automatically identifies videos that are matches or potential matches of a user's content. Anybody with a YouTube account who is in the YouTube Partner Program or has submitted a valid copyright takedown notice is eligible for access to the Copyright Match Tool."],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle2Component1ParagraphTextV7","<ul><li>Uploaders are empowered to push back on removals they believe are invalid by filing counter notifications, and they can push back on Content ID claims by disputing the claim.<li>Of the {contentidclaimcount} Content ID claims made in {year1}, fewer than 1% have been disputed. Over {percentage1} of those disputes resolved in favor of the uploader, either because claimants voluntarily released the claim or did not respond to the dispute in time.</ul>"],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.summary.SectionTitle2Component1ParagraphTextV8","<ul><li>Uploaders are empowered to push back on removals they believe are invalid by filing counter notifications, and they can push back on Content ID claims by disputing the claim.<li>Of the {contentidclaimcount} Content ID claims made in {year1}, fewer than 1% have been disputed. Over {percentage1} of those disputes resolved in favor of the uploader, either because claimants voluntarily released the claim or did not respond to the dispute in time.</ul>"],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.FooterParagraphText1V7","<i><b>Data Collection Note:</b><br>All data in this report is collected between January and December 2024, captured as a snapshot at the beginning of 2025, unless otherwise annotated.</i>"],["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.FooterParagraphText1V8","<i><b>Data Collection Note:</b><br>All data in this report is collected between January and December 2025, captured as a snapshot at the beginning of 2026, unless otherwise annotated.</i>"],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.edge.SectionTitle1Component0ParagraphTextV7",'Our Emmy award-winning Content ID system was the first tool in our Copyright Management Suite to rely on automated detection, and it remains cutting edge today. Based on reference files provided by Content ID partners, YouTube creates digital "fingerprints" for the copyright owner\'s works and conducts automated scans of the platform to determine when content in an uploaded video matches the reference content. When a match is found, Content ID automatically claims the content. Because of continued investment in our matching technology, over 99% of all claims made by Content ID in {year1} were automated.'],
["transparencyReport.youtubecopyright.edge.SectionTitle1Component1ParagraphTextV7","Despite the power of technology, there are some cases where Content ID fails to identify a match with a user video. This can be due to uploaders\u2019 efforts to evade Content ID or due to the fleeting use of the copyrighted work. For videos missed by automated identification, many Content ID partners have the ability to issue claims manually. While this feature covers an important gap, it accounted for fewer than 0.5% of Content ID claims made in {year1}. For music rightsholders in particular, the automation rate is even higher. Finally, all channels on YouTube also have access to our copyright removal webform to request removal of any content not captured by another tool to which they have access."]]);
Yza=[["<b>Remove:</b> The URL was removed from YouTube","A removal request is accepted by YouTube and the video is removed for copyright under the owner name given in the request.<br><br>A removal request is received for a video that\u2019s already been removed from YouTube, either by the uploader or for violating another policy."],["<b>Abuse:</b> A webform submission is deemed by our review team to be a likely false assertion of copyright ownership.","An individual falsely claims to be a celebrity or a large company.<br><br>A creator tries to remove a video competing for the same audience."],
["<b>Invalid Request:</b> There are a number of reasons that requests may be ruled invalid. This may be because the user submitting the request did not provide necessary information even after a clarification request from YouTube, or because they are trying to address a non-copyright issue (like trademark or other content moderation issues) through the copyright webform. ","A fan requests removal on behalf of a creator, but doesn\u2019t appear to be authorized to make claims on their behalf.<br><br>An individual does not provide necessary information to process a request, for example they are not sufficiently clear about what content in the video they are claiming, or fail to provide the URL of the video that they claim is infringing.<br><br>A company asserts their logo is infringed, but the logo is a plain wordmark that is appropriate for a trademark removal notice."],
["<b>Copyright Exceptions:</b> Before submitting a copyright removal request, rightsholders must consider whether fair use, fair dealing, or similar exceptions to copyright may protect the video they wish to remove. In some cases, YouTube asks claimants to confirm they\u2019ve done this analysis. If claimants do not adequately respond, the video is not removed.","A company submits a removal request for a video that uses excerpts of their commercial to criticize their business practices."],["<b>Other:</b> In some cases, we hold a request for further review, send a non-standard response, or follow a slightly different process because the content was provided to us under license. In these situations, we've categorized them as 'Other.' We also categorize as 'Other' if we have inconclusive or insufficient data.",
"A movie producer submits a removal request for a movie, but the movie's distributor (who works with the producer) licensed that video to YouTube."]];
